Rename the local variable 'true' in _XtShellAncestorSensitive.

Shell.c declares a file-local `static Boolean true`, which was legal C when it
was written. On MSYS2 the toolchain reaches this translation unit with
<stdbool.h> already in effect (pulled in through the Windows/Cygwin headers),
where `true` is a macro expanding to 1 - so the declaration becomes
`static Boolean 1 = True;` and the file does not compile.

Renaming the variable is the whole fix: nothing else refers to it, it has
internal linkage, and the address handed back through value->addr is unchanged.

--- a/src/Shell.c
+++ b/src/Shell.c
@@ -1002,10 +1002,10 @@
 static void
 _XtShellAncestorSensitive(Widget widget, int closure, XrmValue *value)
 {
-    static Boolean true = True;
+    static Boolean true_value = True;
 
     if (widget->core.parent == NULL)
-        value->addr = (XPointer) (&true);
+        value->addr = (XPointer) (&true_value);
     else
         _XtCopyFromParent(widget, closure, value);
 }
